{
 "about": "The type encodings of the selectors of the Horos and OsiriX plugin SDK that the application answers as facades, as the Objective-C compiler gives them for the declarations of that SDK's headers on arm64, without the frame offsets. null is a selector whose declaration names a C++ type (a DCMTK, VTK or standard library class), which plain Objective-C cannot declare: it is only asked whether it answers. tests/test-legacy-plugin-selectors.py compares each with the method the running application has. The selectors of Wait the headers of Horos do not declare (+showWithString:, +showWithString:maxProgress:showCancel:, -increment, -indeterminateIndicator, -maxProgress, -run, -setIndeterminate:, -setMaxProgress:, -setProgressValue:, -setString:) have the types of the declarations in the headers the OsiriX SDK publishes as text for plugin developers today (Wait.h in the Headers of its OsiriXAPI.framework), read for names and types; -progress, which those headers and the ones of Horos declare with different classes of indicator, is an object for both. tests/test-wait-panel-former-sdk.py compares the ones of Wait with the panel compiled alone.",
